WEBVTT

NOTE Pro version demo — issue-worm-pro full pipeline
NOTE Transcript: docs/assets/demo-transcripts.md#pro-version-demo

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
This is issue-worm-pro, the full pipeline.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Same starting point: a GitHub issue.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000
But here the scheduler picks it up,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
and the triage step decides whether it's ready to work — is it scoped,
is it actionable, does it need more information first?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Once triage passes, the coder writes the changes.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Then the verifier runs —

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
it checks the coder's work against the issue's DONE: criteria and the
repo's own CI checks.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
If the verifier fails, its feedback goes back to the coder as an
Analyser note, and the coder gets another attempt.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
That loop is bounded — three attempts here — so a genuinely stuck issue
fails cleanly instead of spinning forever.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
When the verifier passes, pro drafts the PR description from the issue
and the diff, opens the PR,

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.000
and updates the issue with a live progress comment as each stage
finishes.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:12.000
So the difference from the free shell is the loop:

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
the free tier writes the code once and hands it back to you;

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:25.000
pro judges its own failures, retries with real feedback, and only opens
the PR once the verifier is satisfied.
